  body: "# Shared additional pension following a pension sharing order\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe RP chapter
    links shared additional pension to a court’s pension sharing order following divorce or civil-partnership dissolution
    and distinguishes associated pension-credit and debit terms.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nShared additional
    pension is a pension-sharing concept, not the Pension Credit means-tested benefit. Old and new state scheme
    pension credits and the relevant court-order and pensionable-age dates require their own legal review.\n\n##
    Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 75611, PDF page 142](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=142).\n\
    - [DMG 75615, PDF page 143](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=143).\n\
    - [DMG 75617, PDF page 143](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=143).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch75` — PDF SHA-256 `655e7acb31f09f5169efbe40419091ee479f88c0c45b65c7a507b042b67712f9`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `0d037880d2aeaff1be89235ee987ca4acb1c839fcf1ead8b8be2daa9f6795465`.\n"
