    rationale: The source defines the valuation day as the day the pension-sharing credit and debit are
      created, rather than the source capture or publication date.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch75/0143
      quote: "75616 The valuation day is the day on which the pension credit and pension debit are created 1. On
        the\nvaluation day the AP belonging to one spouse or civil partner is reduced by the percentage ordered
        by\nthe court and a sum of money equal to the amount of the reduction is deposited in the NI account of
        the\nother spouse or civil partner. This is the old state scheme pension credit.\n\n\n                 \
        \                                                                      1 WRP Act 99, s 49"
